CommitDate: Fri Sep 18 18:56:47 2026 -0500

    fix(userns): state the auto-sandbox degradation cause from the observed probe marker (DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-15)
    
    The fallback warning asserted the uid-mapping/DAC cause unconditionally. That
    is the documented capable-host case — the property probe reports
    `read_rc=1 write_rc=1` there — but the same fallback also triggers when a
    creatable mapped launch fails the property for an unrelated reason (e.g. a
    caller cwd it cannot write), and a warning that names a cause it did not
    measure is the defect class this ticket is about.
    
    The property preflight now returns the marker it observed
    (`_property_observation()`, with `mapped_file_access_ok()` kept as the boolean
    wrapper) and the warning quotes it: the subuid/DAC sentence only for the denied
    marker, otherwise the observed marker (or "no marker") verbatim, so a cause is
    never invented. Selection behaviour and the explicit `--user` path are
    unchanged.
    
    Tests: the capable-host case now also asserts the cause it named (subordinate
    uid), plus two new cases — an observed `read_rc=0 write_rc=1` marker must NOT be
    attributed to the uid mapping, and a marker-less launch is reported as
    "no marker".
    
    Gates: .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q -> 601 passed, 5 skipped;
    uvx ruff check . -> All checks passed!; ruff format --check unchanged from HEAD
    (pre-existing hunks only).
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
